quiet 3000 20000
send Please use the AskUserQuestion tool once with one question, header Next work, multiSelect set to true: which open items should we work on? Four options. Option one, label Claude's screens, description: Put the lines of tab screens like /status and /help in the conversation. Handle /chrome, a new theme in /theme and the commands not known yet. Fix screen titles that pick up a leftover line, such as "Shell details dismissed. Rewind". Option two, label NVDA test run, description: Go through docs/nvda-test-plan.md on the released build together, including the 1.5.0 steps 7 to 9 you had not confirmed yet. I prepare each step, you listen. Option three, label Tool detail key, description: Your idea, not started: one line per tool call, plus a key that unfolds its full output. It works on Claude's --verbose flag. Option four, label Strip-back pass, description: Review menus, options and speech for anything that can go, to keep the app minimal. Do not do anything else and do not read any files.
sleep 200
send \r
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 3000 20000
send \x1b
quiet 3000 20000
send /exit
sleep 200
send \r
exit 10000
